            {
                "content": "# SAN JOAQUIN RIVER BASIN\n\n261\n\n# Chiquito Creek near Arnold Meadow, Calif.\n\nLocation. --Lat 37\u00b024'50\", long. 119\u00b022'50\", in NEt sec. 18, T. 6 S. R. 24 E., on right bank 0.5 mile downstream from Beasore Creek, 0.6 mile southwest of Arnold Meadow, and 12 miles northeast of town of Bass Lake.\n\nRecords available -September 1921 to June 1928, November 1951 to September 1953 (no winter records).\n\nDrainage area.--59.6 sq mi.\n\nGage - -Water-stage recorder. Altitude of gage is 4,800 ft (from topographic map). Prior to Apr. 30, 1922, staff gage at same site and datum.\n\nAverage discharge --6 years (1921-27), 88.2 cfs.\n\nExtremes. --1951-52: Maximum discharge recorded during period November to September, 1,470 cfs May 27 (gage height, 9.13 ft); minimum, 6.8 cfs Nov. 8-11. height, 7.79 ft); minimum, 4.3 cfs Sept. 29. 1952-53: Maximum discharge recorded during water year, 800 cfs Apr. 27 (gage 1921-28, 1951-53: Maximum discharge recorded, that of May 27, 1952; minimum, 1.4 cfs Aug. 27-31, 1924.\n\nRemarks. --Records good except those for periods of no gage-height record, which are fair. No storage or diversion.",
